{"name":"Blue Fire","hex":"#00aadd","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue fire","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Sensational romanticism.","A fire that burns a blue color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_fire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Fire megacoaster is a launched roller coaster at Europa-Park. The coaster opened in 2009 as part of a new Iceland-themed expansion to Europa-Park. As the first launched coaster built by Mack Rides, Blue Fire was the park's tenth roller coaster and the first to feature inversions. Originally, the ride was sponsored by Gazprom, but after the invasion of Ukraine launched by Russia on 24th February 2022, the sponsorship was dropped, due to Gazprom being owned by the Russian government. The ride's tagline is \"Discover Pure Energy\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Blue_Fire_Megacoaster_-_Europa-Park_-_Durchfahrt_des_Loopings.jpg/330px-Blue_Fire_Megacoaster_-_Europa-Park_-_Durchfahrt_des_Loopings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Fire","wikidata":"Q477897"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire","wikidata":"Q3196"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Europa-Park_-_Blue_Fire_Megacoaster_%2821%29.JPG/250px-Europa-Park_-_Blue_Fire_Megacoaster_%2821%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Europa-Park_-_Blue_Fire_Megacoaster_%2821%29.JPG/330px-Europa-Park_-_Blue_Fire_Megacoaster_%2821%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Europa-Park_-_Blue_Fire_Megacoaster_%2821%29.JPG/250px-Europa-Park_-_Blue_Fire_Megacoaster_%2821%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEuropa-Park_-_Blue_Fire_Megacoaster_(21).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/EP_bluefire.jpg/250px-EP_bluefire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped